  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting gender equality with church partners - general</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Research and learning exchange:
A pivotal element of the overall programme is to support exchange of learning between partners to increase quality of gender work through engaging with church structures effectively. This will involve the exchange and documentation of experience of all participating partners. Initial research and documentation will be undertaken with the Philippines partner Sabakan to identify learning, effective strategies and recommendations which will be shared with the other participating partners during the learning exchange workshop and within CAFOD to inform the ongoing programme. The exchange and learning event between the participating partners and faith leaders from each country will take place in Kenya in June 2013. Partners will be attending from Zambia, Zimbabwe, Mozambique, Philippines and Kenya.  The workshop is for 3 days: the first 2 days focused on church and gender resource partners learning and discussion and the third day will be a practical visit to a selected Kenya partner for peer review.</narrative>
  </description>
